IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dcm-rules`

-- Diplomatic and Consular Missions Act 1978 (Cth) — the encoder's tests.

§ `Tests`

`consented` MEANS `a diplomatic or consular mission of a country, established in Australia with the Commonwealth's consent`
`designated` MEANS `a designated overseas mission of a foreign territory`
`sign` MEANS `displaying a sign, flag or insignia, or causing or permitting it`
`claim` MEANS `making or publishing a representation, or causing or permitting it`

GIVEN m IS A `Mission concerned`, k IS A `Conduct`, prem IS A BOOLEAN, imp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Missions case`
`a case about` m `by` k `at mission premises` prem `implying` imp MEANS
    `Missions case` OF m, k, prem, imp, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, JUST (Date 15 3 2026)

-- s 4(2)(a): a sign elsewhere than the mission's premises.
#ASSERT `my conduct is caught` (`a case about` `consented` `by` `sign` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`my conduct is caught` (`a case about` `consented` `by` `sign` `at mission premises` TRUE `implying` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`my conduct is caught` (`a case about` `consented` `by` `sign` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` FALSE))
-- s 4(2)(b)
#ASSERT `my conduct is caught` (`a case about` `consented` `by` `claim` `at mission premises` TRUE `implying` TRUE)
-- s 4(2A), (2B)
#ASSERT `my conduct is caught` (`a case about` `designated` `by` `sign` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` TRUE)
#ASSERT `my conduct is caught` (`a case about` `designated` `by` `claim` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`my conduct is caught` (`a case about` `no such mission` `by` `claim` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` TRUE))
-- s 4(2)(c)-(d), (2A)(e)
#ASSERT NOT (`my conduct is caught` (`Missions case` OF `consented`, `sign`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`my conduct is caught` (`Missions case` OF `designated`, `sign`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING))
-- s 4(5)-(6)
#ASSERT `an injunction may be granted` (`a case about` `consented` `by` `sign` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` TRUE)
#ASSERT `an injunction may be granted` (`Missions case` OF `consented`, `claim`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`an injunction may be granted` (`Missions case` OF `consented`, `claim`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING))
-- s 5(1): only for signs.
#ASSERT `a removal warrant may issue` (`a case about` `consented` `by` `sign` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a removal warrant may issue` (`a case about` `consented` `by` `claim` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` TRUE))
-- s 5(5): issued 15 March 2026, in force at most to 14 September 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day of a removal warrant` (`a case about` `consented` `by` `sign` `at mission premises` FALSE `implying` TRUE) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 9 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day of a removal warrant` (`Missions case` OF `consented`, `sign`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, JUST (Date 31 8 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2027)
